# material_concepts.pdl - D35 M3: what each material LOOKS like (the attention keys) and which words pull toward it (the biases). HAND-SET by claude 2026-11-05 under the owner's 2026-11-06 delegation ("u can review weights and even hand tune biases"). Edit freely; the studio writes its own overrides to state/studio_bias.pdl and never this file.
# DIMS: warm wet wear grain edge round metal big worn, each -1..+1 (same order as concept-bank/data/hidden/look_assoc.*).
# KEY | material | 9 numbers in DIMS order                 the key vector k_m of the attention
# BIAS | material | b                                       a prior added to the score of that material (default 0)
# WORDAFF | word | material | affinity 0..1                 a word in the phrase adds `affinity * word_gain` to that material's score; plural s is tried too
